The Option ROM for the following device could not be dumped to disk:
%1

This could mean that the device does not actually have an Option ROM of its own
but is part of the chipset. In that case, it does not have a signature that
needs to be verified and should therefore work fine, regardless of what the keys
the user enrolls. However, it could also mean something else entirely and it is
recommended to research the device and the machine itself online to safeguard
against any issues that might occur when using Secure Boot.
